LLM-Answer:
Using \(\displaystyle \lim_{u\to0}\frac{\sin u}{u}=1\), set \(u=3x\):

\[
\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin(3x)}{x}
=3\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin(3x)}{3x}
=3.
\]

By Vieta’s formulas, \(\alpha+\beta=\frac{7}{2}\) and \(\alpha\beta=\frac{3}{2}\). Therefore,
\[
\frac{1}{\alpha}+\frac{1}{\beta}
=\frac{\alpha+\beta}{\alpha\beta}
=\frac{7/2}{3/2}
=\boxed{\frac{7}{3}}.
\]

Using \(\displaystyle \lim_{u\to 0}\frac{\sin u}{u}=1\), let \(u=3x\). Then
\[
\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin(3x)}{x}
=3\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin(3x)}{3x}
=3.
\]
